/-!
# Human-readable axiom report, and the gate that reads it

This module pins the axiom reports for the public results and the three most
load-bearing mathematical inputs.  It is imported by the library root, so a
normal `lake build` prints these reports.

Every line below is `#audit_axioms` rather than `#print axioms`: the report is
printed exactly as before, and the command additionally **fails the build** if
the closure leaves `propext / Classical.choice / Quot.sound`.  See
`GroupApproximation/Meta/AxiomGuard.lean` for why that matters -- five hundred
`#print axioms` lines describe the trust surface without gating it, and a
widened closure was previously only a line of log output.

The stricter executable gate in `scripts/Audit.lean` independently traverses
the transitive axiom closure of every declaration of the corpus, including the
ones no line here names, and fails on anything beyond classical Lean.  The two
are deliberately redundant: this one cannot be skipped, that one cannot be
escaped by not being cited.
-/

